{"created": "2026-10-09T15:21:08.540550+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-09T15:23:13.879911+00:00", "id": 23265728, "conceptrecid": "23261743", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23265728", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23261743", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23265728", "metadata": {"title": "Weil positivity on the window of width log 12, and a lower bound for the prolate eigenvalue defect", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23265728", "publication_date": "2026-10-10", "description": "<p>Weil's criterion states that the Riemann Hypothesis holds if and only if Weil's quadratic form Q is nonnegative on all admissible test functions. Restricting the support to a fixed interval [&minus;L, L] gives a weaker, unconditional question. We prove that Q(f) &ge; 2<sup>&minus;1518</sup>&Vert;f&Vert;<sub>2</sub><sup>2</sup> for every complex C<sup>2</sup> function f supported in [&minus;&frac12;log 12, &frac12;log 12]; the half-width &frac12;log 12 &asymp; 1.2425 exceeds that of the previous proofs we know of, the largest being &frac12;log 10 (our previous paper). The new analytic ingredient is an explicit lower bound for the defect of the top eigenvalue of time and frequency limiting: 1 &minus; &lambda;<sub>0</sub>(c) &ge; e<sup>&minus;2(c+1)</sup>/(4(c+1)(c+4)) for all c &gt; 0, which has the correct exponential rate e<sup>&minus;2c</sup>. It replaces the out-of-band estimate of our previous paper, which was proved under the convenient hypothesis L &lt; 7/6, and it improves the constant on the window of half-width &frac12;log 10 from 2<sup>&minus;49162</sup> to 2<sup>&minus;876</sup> without recomputing the finite matrices. The proof follows Liu's bounded-comparison framework and reduces positivity to a finite matrix inequality of size 416 in each parity, which we certify in Arb ball arithmetic with all quadrature, rounding and inversion errors paid: the finite margin is about 1.21&times;10<sup>&minus;54</sup> (even) and 1.59&times;10<sup>&minus;50</sup> (odd), while the total error is below 10<sup>&minus;75</sup>. It is an external certificate, not a formal proof. The result concerns one fixed window and does not address the Riemann Hypothesis.</p><p>Certificate code and data: folder certificate-VII of release v1.5.1 of https://github.com/moriryota/prolate-weil-bounds (all versions: doi:10.5281/zenodo.23092422).</p><p>Version 2 (10 October 2026) defines the functions b<sub>j</sub> used in the quadrature lemma and the sign of the transform in the projection lemma, adds the identity behind W(X) &#x2AB0; G, and refers to release v1.5.1, which corrects the replay instructions of the certificate. The theorems and all constants are unchanged.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Mori, Ryota", "affiliation": "Independent researcher, Tokyo, Japan"}], "keywords": ["Riemann Hypothesis", "Weil positivity", "Weil explicit formula", "Riemann zeta function", "prolate spheroidal wave functions", "time and frequency limiting", "eigenvalue defect", "ball arithmetic", "computer-assisted proof"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23238480", "relation": "continues", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23092422", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23175061", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23092454", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23035705", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "arXiv:2608.24827", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "arxiv"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/luciferyu666/certified-weil-positivity", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "2", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": false, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23261743"}}]}}, "title": "Weil positivity on the window of width log 12, and a lower bound for the prolate eigenvalue defect", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23265728", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23265728", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23265728?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23265728", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23265728", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23265728", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23265728/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23261743", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23261743", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23261743", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23261743", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23265728/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23265728/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23265728/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23265728/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23265728:mori-paper-VII.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23265728:mori-paper-VII.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23265728:mori-paper-VII.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23265728:mori-paper-VII.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23265728:mori-paper-VII.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23265728:mori-paper-VII.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23265728/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/re